24 Nov 2026: dvdrental practice and fixing my queries

What I learned:

Before grouping by a date, decide the level you want (day, month or year) and cut the date down to it first. DATE_TRUNC('month', rental_date) groups by month and keeps the year. (Not covered properly yet, so I'm coming back to it.)
Always GROUP BY the ID as well as the name (e.g. customer_id, first_name, last_name), so two people with the same name don't get merged.
Only join the tables you actually need. In the category revenue query I could skip film and join film_category straight to inventory.
DBeaver auto-commits by default, so UPDATE and DELETE can't be undone with Cmd + Z. Switch to manual commit to be able to ROLLBACK.

What tripped me up:

