I joined payment on customer_id instead of rental_id. That attached every payment a customer made to every film they rented, so all the totals were inflated.
One query answered a different question from the one I'd written in the comment. Lesson: before writing, decide what the answer should look like: one number, one row per film, or one row per customer?
Mixing aliased and unaliased tables in the same query.

