Nov 2026: SQLBolt lessons 7–8: outer joins, NULLs and DISTINCT

What I learned:

Outer joins: LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, FULL JOIN
When tables have asymmetric data (e.g. a brand with no products yet), use LEFT/RIGHT/FULL JOIN so nothing gets left out
Whatever comes after FROM is the left table, and whatever comes after JOIN is the right table
We mostly use LEFT JOIN because it's easier to read from left to right; a RIGHT JOIN can be rewritten as a LEFT JOIN by swapping the tables
To check for missing values, use IS NULL / IS NOT NULL, never = NULL
DISTINCT comes straight after SELECT

