19 Nov 2026: sorting, LIMIT/OFFSET and INNER JOIN

What I learned:

DISTINCT removes duplicate rows, so you only see unique entries (still working on explaining it clearly)
ORDER BY is used with ASC / DESC
LIMIT = how many rows you want; OFFSET = how many rows you skip first
Example: when you open Pinterest, the first screen shows the top 25 pins (LIMIT 25 OFFSET 0). When you scroll, it fetches the next 25 (LIMIT 25 OFFSET 25), skipping the first 25.
Tables are combined with INNER JOIN, and ON says which columns link them (usually a primary key in one table to a foreign key in the other)
Everything learned before (WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT) still works after a join

